WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.901 --> 00:00:03.701
-Hey, Doc?
-Mm-hmm?

00:00:03.701 --> 00:00:08.567
-I know it's Thursday,
but I was thinking tonight

00:00:08.567 --> 00:00:13.300
could be a-a good night
for sex night possibly.

00:00:14.968 --> 00:00:17.067
-Ooh.

00:00:17.067 --> 00:00:21.534
It's an interesting idea,
but, you know...

00:00:21.534 --> 00:00:24.000
Thursdays.

00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:25.234
-Welcome back to "Late Night."

00:00:25.234 --> 00:00:28.000
We're here with Anne Hathaway,
everybody!

00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:30.868
That was a clip
from "She Came to Me."

00:00:30.868 --> 00:00:33.100
And you --
Your wonderful co-star,

00:00:33.100 --> 00:00:35.467
Peter Dinklage, he plays --
what would you call it --

00:00:35.467 --> 00:00:37.267
opera composer?
-Yes.

00:00:37.267 --> 00:00:39.033
-Yes.
-He plays an opera composer

00:00:39.033 --> 00:00:42.434
who is on year five
of an artistic blockage.

00:00:42.434 --> 00:00:44.300
-Gotcha.
And you play a therapist?

00:00:44.300 --> 00:00:45.701
-I was his therapist.
-Okay.

00:00:45.701 --> 00:00:47.968
-And then we got married.
-Oh, that's always good.

00:00:47.968 --> 00:00:50.901
-They say that you should
definitely do that.

00:00:50.901 --> 00:00:53.267
-And one day,
I'm feeling a little --

00:00:53.267 --> 00:00:56.567
I'm feeling like I need
a little bit of space from him.

00:00:56.567 --> 00:00:58.667
And so I send him off on a walk,

00:00:58.667 --> 00:01:00.300
and I tell him
to interact with a stranger,

00:01:00.300 --> 00:01:01.934
and he winds up
meeting Marisa Tomei,

00:01:01.934 --> 00:01:03.434
who's a tugboat captain,

00:01:03.434 --> 00:01:05.567
and she takes him
back to her tugboat

00:01:05.567 --> 00:01:08.167
where she reveals to him
while disrobing

00:01:08.167 --> 00:01:11.200
that she is
a sex and love addict.

00:01:11.200 --> 00:01:12.901
-Oh, wow.
-Yes.

00:01:12.901 --> 00:01:15.934
-So never tell your spouse
to take a walk.

00:01:15.934 --> 00:01:17.968
You never know --
never know what might happen.

00:01:17.968 --> 00:01:20.868
-Well, just when you feel
really sorry for my character,

00:01:20.868 --> 00:01:23.167
because she is successful
in seducing him,

00:01:23.167 --> 00:01:25.033
you realize that I am

00:01:25.033 --> 00:01:27.133
actually in a secret
relationship with God.

00:01:27.133 --> 00:01:29.033
-Oh! Well, there you go!

00:01:29.033 --> 00:01:30.968
It's so what I love
about indie movies.

00:01:30.968 --> 00:01:32.300
[ Laughter ]

00:01:32.300 --> 00:01:34.067
Did you enjoy
playing a therapist?

00:01:34.067 --> 00:01:35.901
-I did.
I did enjoy playing a therapist.

00:01:35.901 --> 00:01:37.534
I was really nervous
about, like,

00:01:37.534 --> 00:01:39.067
you know,
just getting it right

00:01:39.067 --> 00:01:40.567
and making sure --
it can be quite serious.

00:01:40.567 --> 00:01:42.434
But yeah, yeah, it felt like

00:01:42.434 --> 00:01:45.534
I could put a lot of things
I have learned to use.

00:01:45.534 --> 00:01:47.901
-Yeah, that would be my fear,
if I ever played a therapist,

00:01:47.901 --> 00:01:51.267
is that one of mine would go,
"Is that me?"

00:01:51.267 --> 00:01:53.100
You had a really a cool thing,
which is --

00:01:53.100 --> 00:01:54.968
Again, we mentioned
that you're a producer.

00:01:54.968 --> 00:01:56.934
One of the things
you have to do is reach out,

00:01:56.934 --> 00:01:59.100
try to find people
to help you with your movie.

00:01:59.100 --> 00:02:01.634
For the soundtrack,
you had somebody write a song.

00:02:01.634 --> 00:02:04.534
-Yes, yes, yes. Rebecca was the
one that reached out to him.

00:02:04.534 --> 00:02:06.801
But our title song,
the end-credits song,

00:02:06.801 --> 00:02:08.167
is written by Bruce Springsteen.

00:02:08.167 --> 00:02:09.801
-That's really incredible.
-I know!

00:02:09.801 --> 00:02:11.667
-And the day you find out
that he's gonna do it,

00:02:11.667 --> 00:02:14.534
it just must be --
What a celebration.

00:02:14.534 --> 00:02:16.701
-I mean, it was kind of one of
those moments that was so cool.

00:02:16.701 --> 00:02:18.634
You expect, like,
everything to explode,

00:02:18.634 --> 00:02:21.133
but instead it goes quiet.
You know what I mean?

00:02:21.133 --> 00:02:25.267
Like, it's so --
it's so impossible to imagine.

00:02:25.267 --> 00:02:28.567
He's -- Yeah, he's so mythic
in his -- in his way.

00:02:28.567 --> 00:02:30.567
-Yes. And very sage.
When you actually talk to him,

00:02:30.567 --> 00:02:32.334
he seems to have
a very deep wisdom

00:02:32.334 --> 00:02:33.701
that not a lot of people have.

00:02:33.701 --> 00:02:36.000
-Oh. my gosh. I couldn't.
I couldn't talk to him.

00:02:36.000 --> 00:02:38.567
I couldn't possibly do it.

00:02:38.567 --> 00:02:39.934
-Yeah, the first time I met him,

00:02:39.934 --> 00:02:42.701
he did music
my first year on "SNL."

00:02:42.701 --> 00:02:44.067
And I just had to do that thing,

00:02:44.067 --> 00:02:46.334
which is I had to just --
I had to say a thing to him

00:02:46.334 --> 00:02:48.467
that he's heard a hundred times
and just walk over and be like,

00:02:48.467 --> 00:02:50.067
"Hey, I just want to say..."

00:02:50.067 --> 00:02:52.133
And he was like, "Cool. How's
the show gonna be this week?"

00:02:52.133 --> 00:02:53.901
And I just like, "Uh..."
And just walked away.

00:02:53.901 --> 00:02:55.667
I was like, "Oh, I'm not ready

00:02:55.667 --> 00:02:57.334
to have, like,
a back-and-forth here.

00:02:57.334 --> 00:02:59.067
This isn't a conversation.

00:02:59.067 --> 00:03:01.501
This is me unburdening and
running away as fast as I can."

00:03:01.501 --> 00:03:04.100
-I just also love the way
you so casually just said,

00:03:04.100 --> 00:03:06.000
"Yeah, Bruce Springsteen
was the musical guest

00:03:06.000 --> 00:03:08.501
the first week
that I was on 'SNL.'"

00:03:08.501 --> 00:03:10.400
Like, you just dropped that
so casually.

00:03:10.400 --> 00:03:11.834
Do you ever hear yourself?

00:03:11.834 --> 00:03:13.200
-It was my second season.
He was the first.

00:03:13.200 --> 00:03:15.000
-Oh, it was your second.
Okay. Got it. Got it. Got it.

00:03:15.000 --> 00:03:16.601
-I don't remember
all of the musical guests,

00:03:16.601 --> 00:03:18.701
but I remember that,
and I remember The Killers

00:03:18.701 --> 00:03:20.200
'cause they're still on the lam.

00:03:20.200 --> 00:03:21.734
[ Laughter ]

00:03:21.734 --> 00:03:24.567
You've had time on.
I know you love Broadway.

00:03:24.567 --> 00:03:26.534
You are a theater kid,
through and through.

00:03:26.534 --> 00:03:28.868
-It's true. It's true.
-Have you managed to see stuff

00:03:28.868 --> 00:03:30.701
during this downtime?
-Oh!

00:03:30.701 --> 00:03:33.601
I saw -- A few months ago now,

00:03:33.601 --> 00:03:37.133
but I saw my wonderful friend
Jessica Chastain,

00:03:37.133 --> 00:03:39.400
like, levitate on stage
in "A Doll's House."

00:03:39.400 --> 00:03:40.734
Did anybody here get to see it?

00:03:40.734 --> 00:03:41.968
-[ Cheers and applause ]
-[ Gasps ]

00:03:41.968 --> 00:03:43.467
It's like nothing
I've ever seen.

00:03:43.467 --> 00:03:45.834
She was -- She was -- I mean,
just -- She was everything.

00:03:45.834 --> 00:03:47.667
And then it's so cool
that David Byr--

00:03:47.667 --> 00:03:49.801
I mean, for so many reasons
it's so cool that
David Byrne is here,

00:03:49.801 --> 00:03:51.501
but I can't wait
to see "Here Lies Love."

00:03:51.501 --> 00:03:53.234
I got to see it at the Public.
-Oh, my gosh.

00:03:53.234 --> 00:03:54.801
-During the first run of it.

00:03:54.801 --> 00:03:57.868
And so I'm so excited to go see
it, just as soon as we're done.

00:03:57.868 --> 00:03:59.901
-Alright. Well, I am
so happy to have you here.

00:03:59.901 --> 00:04:01.834
It's always just such a delight
to see you.

00:04:01.834 --> 00:04:03.901
Congratulations on the film.
-Thank you so much.

00:04:03.901 --> 00:04:06.667
-And we always want you
to come back.

00:04:06.667 --> 00:04:09.767
Anne Hathaway. "She Came to Me"
is in theaters October 6th.

00:04:09.767 --> 00:04:12.133
Stick around. We'll be
right back with David Byrne.

